-- title:
--   Supersingular closed points contract along maps of j-chart rings
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, local rings $A_0$ and $A$ with $A$ an $A_0$-algebra whose structure map is local, and assume $q$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $F_0$ be a field with an $A_0$-algebra structure and $j_0 \in F_0$ non-zero, and $F$ a field with an $A$-algebra structure and $j \in F$ non-zero; write $C_0 =$ `chartAlgFin A₀ F₀ j₀` for the subalgebra of $F_0$ of elements integral over $A_0[j_0]$, and $C =$ `chartAlgFin A F j` likewise inside $F$, with `jChartFin` denoting $j_0 \in C_0$ and $j \in C$. Let $c : C_0 \to C$ be a ring homomorphism with $c(j_0) = j$ which is compatible with $A_0 \to A$, i.e. $c(a \cdot 1) = (\text{image of } a \text{ in } A) \cdot 1$ for all $a \in A_0$. Let $y \subset C$ be a maximal ideal containing the ideal generated by the image of the maximal ideal of $A$, and suppose $j$ is supersingular at $y$: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of $j$-invariants such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no non-zero point killed by $q$. Finally let $\varpi_0$ be an element of the maximal ideal of $A_0$. The conclusion is threefold: $c^{-1}(y)$ is a maximal ideal of $C_0$; the image of $\varpi_0$ in $C_0$ lies in $c^{-1}(y)$; and for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi_0 : C_0 \to \Omega$ with kernel $c^{-1}(y)$, one has $\varphi_0(j_0) \in$ [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7).
--
--   This is the descent step for supersingular closed points on the $j$-finite chart of the two-chart integral model: a supersingular closed point of the chart over $A$ contracts, along a map of chart rings compatible with a local extension of the ring of constants, to a supersingular closed point of the chart over $A_0$, maximality being preserved because the residue field extension is integral. It is used in the construction of chart rings with prescribed cyclotomic constants for the auxiliary full-level modular curves.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel_isMaximal_comap_and_mem_comap_and_mem_ssJSet_of_ringHom_chartAlgFin.lean

